From 0c58a20324a400dd34a966a07fd86919183143ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:06:31 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(post): state each Sodick condition's kerf gap and
 flag example rows

The Wire Contour offset is the wire radius plus the condition gap, and
the Sodick post writes no G41 / G42. The posted program now states the
gap of each condition it selects (the cut and each skim), so the
operator can compare it with the control's row. A row whose notes start
with EXAMPLE gets a WARNING note that names the example gap and says to
replace it before cutting.

The wire machine mirror carries edm.conditions when the file states a
table, so the post can read the gap. Goldens moved: the four
sodick-wire programs gain the note lines only.

Refs #3214

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
